  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MATOPOS NATIONAL PARK: ANNUAL DARTING AND IMMOBILISATION OF BLACK AND WHITE RHINO FOR ROUTINE DEHORNING AND EAR-NOTCHING TO AID MONITORING AND PROTECTION STRATEGIES</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO SUPPORT A CONSERVATION EFFORT IN MATOPOS NATIONAL PARK, ZIMBABWE BY AIDING POPULATION MONITORING AND PROTECTION STRATEGIES. THIS PROJECT IS INTENDED TO CONSERVE RHINOCEROS AND THEIR HABITAT BY ADDRESSING THE IMPACTS OF TARGETED POACHING. SPECIFIC ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: (1) ORGANIZING RHINOCEROS MANAGEMENT OPERATIONS WITH GOVERNMENT PARTNERS (2) SUPPORTING TECHNICAL PERSONNEL (3) IMMOBILIZING RHINOCEROS FOR DEHORNING AND EAR-NOTCHING AND (4) COLLECTING BIOMETRIC DATA TO INFORM POPULATION MANAGEMENT.</narrative>
  </description>
